+# Local Agent Plugins fixture
+
+This package exercises the local-only Agent Plugins 1.0.0 adapter against
+<https://agent-plugins.org/specification>. It has no code plugin entrypoint.
+The MCP command is only a configuration fixture; `server.cjs` is intentionally absent.
+
+Configure its directory in `plugins`, or place it beneath `.opencode/plugin/` or
+`.opencode/plugins/`. Root `plugin.json` takes precedence over code entrypoints;
+an invalid manifest fails loading. Unknown manifest fields are reported and ignored.
+Metadata is validated by type, not by URL, email, or semver conventions. Client
+extensions are ignored. Only immediate `skills/*/SKILL.md` children are discovered.
+
+The adapter supports stdio MCP entries in this exact portable envelope:
+
+```json
+{
+  "$schema": "https://agent-plugins.org/schemas/1.0.0/mcp.schema.json",
+  "mcpServers": {
+    "example": { "type": "stdio", "command": "node", "args": ["example.js"] }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Mapping to `Mcp.ServerConfig`: `stdio` becomes `local`, `command` plus `args`
+become the native `command` array, `env` becomes `environment`, and `cwd` becomes
+an absolute contained working directory (default: plugin root). `${PLUGIN_ROOT}`
+and `${PLUGIN_DATA}` expand once in args, environment values and cwd, never in
+command or environment keys. Other placeholders stay literal. Reserved environment
+variables are supplied by the host. Persistent data lives in the OpenCode data
+directory under `agent-plugins/<hash-of-resolved-plugin-root>`.
+
+Remote transports (`streamable-http` and `sse`) are skipped with a diagnostic:
+the native remote config cannot enforce their declared initial transport.
+Invalid MCP files disable MCP only; invalid server entries and skills are skipped
+individually. Package paths are checked using real paths, including symlinks;
+command arguments and environment values remain opaque rather than package paths.
+Contributions are scoped transforms, not copied configuration, and disappear on unload.
